# F1.4 — one line ending, independent of who checks this out or how their
# `core.autocrlf` is set.
#
# Before this file existed, every blob in the repository was already LF (git
# normalizes on commit), but a Windows checkout with the ordinary
# `core.autocrlf=true` silently converted every one of them to CRLF on disk —
# with nothing recording that this was supposed to happen, or supposed not to.
# The measurable effect: `prettier --check` (and therefore `pnpm format:check`
# and `pnpm check`) failed on files nobody had touched, because Prettier's
# default `endOfLine` is `lf` and the working tree held CRLF. This was
# reproduced on a real Windows checkout of this repository before this file
# was added — see docs/development/infrastructure-foundation-report.md, F1.4.
#
# `eol=lf` forces LF at checkout regardless of `core.autocrlf`, so
# `format:check` and `git diff --check` see the same bytes on every platform.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Known binaries — excluded from the text/eol rule above so line-ending
# normalization never touches them. `text=auto`'s own heuristic usually gets
# this right on its own; naming them is what makes it not depend on guessing.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.docx binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.rar binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
